<h1>About CSBFP</h1>
<p class="lead">Certified Small Business Finance Professional (CSBFP) is a professional certification for individuals working in U.S. small business finance.</p>

<h2>Who it's for</h2>
<p>Brokers, funders, lenders, underwriters, operations and servicing staff, compliance and risk professionals, managers, and people entering the industry.</p>

<h2>What it shows</h2>
<p>A CSBFP certification confirms that an individual has completed industry training, passed an assessment covering commercial financing products, applicable laws and professional conduct, and satisfied a one-time background screening requirement.</p>
<p>Each certified individual receives a permanent certification number that can be <a href="/verify">publicly verified</a>.</p>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ol class="numbered">
  <li>Create an account and complete your application.</li>
  <li>Accept the professional standards.</li>
  <li>Complete four short training modules.</li>
  <li>Pass a 20-question assessment.</li>
  <li>Pay the <%= program.annualFee %> annual certification fee.</li>
  <li>Complete a one-time background screening.</li>
  <li>Receive your certification number upon approval.</li>
</ol>

<h2>What it isn't</h2>
<p>CSBFP is a private industry certification. It is not a government license or regulatory approval, and it does not authorize anyone to perform activities that require a license.</p>

